IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `coa-core`

-- coa4-declaration.l4: Companies Act 2006 (United Kingdom), Part 10, Chapter 3: Declaration of interest in existing
-- transaction or arrangement (ss 182 to 187), lines 2412-2465 of ukpga-2006-46.txt. Layer 1 (the law, objectively).
--
-- SOURCE and HOW TO READ AN ANSWER: as in coa4-requirements.l4. Every branch carries its FALSE-kind or NOTHING-kind comment.
-- "as soon as is reasonably practicable" (s 182(4)) and "reasonable steps" (s 185(4)(b)) are open-textured: plain inputs.
-- Naming: every top-level name begins with the label of the provision it implements.

-- ---- s 182: declaration of interest in existing transaction or arrangement --------------------------------------

-- (5): "This section does not require a declaration of an interest of which the director is not aware or where the director is
-- not aware of the transaction or arrangement in question. For this purpose a director is treated as being aware of matters
-- of which he ought reasonably to be aware."
-- src:2423 | (5) This section does not require a declaration of an interest of which the director is not aware or where the director is not aware of the transaction or arrangement in question.
-- src:2424 | For this purpose a director is treated as being aware of matters of which he ought reasonably to be aware.
@ref s 182(5) Awareness (src:2423-2424)
GIVEN `the director is aware of the interest` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the director ought reasonably to be aware of the interest` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the director is aware of the transaction or arrangement in question` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the director ought reasonably to be aware of the transaction or arrangement in question` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 182(5) the section requires a declaration so far as the director's awareness goes` MEANS
    IF       (`the director is aware of the interest` OR `the director ought reasonably to be aware of the interest`)
         AND (`the director is aware of the transaction or arrangement in question` OR `the director ought reasonably to be aware of the transaction or arrangement in question`)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "This section does not require a declaration of an interest of which the director is not aware or where the director is not aware of the transaction or arrangement in question."

-- (6): "A director need not declare an interest under this section (a) if it cannot reasonably be regarded as likely to give rise
-- to a conflict of interest; (b) if, or to the extent that, the other directors are already aware of it ...; or (c) if, or to the
-- extent that, it concerns terms of his service contract that have been or are to be considered (i) by a meeting of the
-- directors, or (ii) by a committee of the directors appointed for the purpose under the company's constitution."
-- src:2425 | (6) A director need not declare an interest under this section—
-- src:2426 | (a) if it cannot reasonably be regarded as likely to give rise to a conflict of interest;
-- src:2427 | (b) if, or to the extent that, the other directors are already aware of it (and for this purpose the other directors are treated as aware of anything of which they ought reasonably to be aware); or
-- src:2428 | (c) if, or to the extent that, it concerns terms of his service contract that have been or are to be considered—
-- src:2429 | (i) by a meeting of the directors, or
-- src:2430 | (ii) by a committee of the directors appointed for the purpose under the company's constitution.
@ref s 182(6) Interests that need not be declared (src:2425-2430)
GIVEN `the interest cannot reasonably be regarded as likely to give rise to a conflict of interest` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the other directors are already aware of it` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the other directors ought reasonably to be aware of it` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it concerns terms of the director's service contract that have been or are to be considered by a meeting of the directors` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it concerns terms of the director's service contract that have been or are to be considered by a committee of the directors appointed for the purpose under the company's constitution` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 182(6) the director need not declare the interest under section 182` MEANS
    IF       `the interest cannot reasonably be regarded as likely to give rise to a conflict of interest`
         OR  `the other directors are already aware of it`
         OR  `the other directors ought reasonably to be aware of it`
         OR  `it concerns terms of the director's service contract that have been or are to be considered by a meeting of the directors`
         OR  `it concerns terms of the director's service contract that have been or are to be considered by a committee of the directors appointed for the purpose under the company's constitution`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "A director need not declare an interest under this section— (a) if it cannot reasonably be regarded as likely to give rise to a conflict of interest"

-- (1): the duty to declare an interest in a transaction or arrangement already entered into, unless the interest has been
-- declared under s 177; (5) and (6) are the answers above.
-- src:2413 | 182 Declaration of interest in existing transaction or arrangement
-- src:2414 | (1) Where a director of a company is in any way, directly or indirectly, interested in a transaction or arrangement that has been entered into by the company, he must declare the nature and extent of the interest to the other directors in accordance with this section.
-- src:2415 | This section does not apply if or to the extent that the interest has been declared under section 177 (duty to declare interest in proposed transaction or arrangement).
@ref s 182(1) Declaration of interest in existing transaction or arrangement (src:2413-2415)
GIVEN `the director is in any way, directly or indirectly, interested in a transaction or arrangement that has been entered into by the company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the interest has been declared under section 177` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the answer under section 182(5)` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the answer under section 182(6)` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 182(1) the director is obliged to declare the nature and extent of the interest to the other directors` MEANS
    IF NOT (`the director is in any way, directly or indirectly, interested in a transaction or arrangement that has been entered into by the company`)
    THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Where a director of a company is in any way, directly or indirectly, interested in a transaction or arrangement that has been entered into by the company"
    ELSE IF `the interest has been declared under section 177`
         THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "This section does not apply if or to the extent that the interest has been declared under section 177"
         ELSE CONSIDER `the answer under section 182(5)`
              WHEN JUST FALSE THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "This section does not require a declaration of an interest of which the director is not aware"
              WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): whether the director is aware is not known
              WHEN JUST TRUE THEN
                   CONSIDER `the answer under section 182(6)`
                   WHEN JUST TRUE THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "A director need not declare an interest under this section"
                   WHEN JUST FALSE THEN JUST TRUE
                   WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): whether an exception in subsection (6) applies is not known

-- (2): "The declaration must be made (a) at a meeting of the directors, or (b) by notice in writing (see section 184), or (c) by
-- general notice (see section 185)." Subsection (2)(a) does not apply to a shadow director (s 187(2)).
-- src:2416 | (2) The declaration must be made—
-- src:2417 | (a) at a meeting of the directors, or
-- src:2418 | (b) by notice in writing (see section 184), or
-- src:2419 | (c) by general notice (see section 185).
@ref s 182(2) How the declaration must be made (src:2416-2419)
GIVEN `the declaration is made at a meeting of the directors` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is a shadow director, so that section 187(2) disapplies subsection (2)(a)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `s 184 the notice in writing is in accordance with section 184` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `s 185 the general notice is in accordance with section 185` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 182(2) the declaration is made in a way the subsection requires` MEANS
    IF (`the declaration is made at a meeting of the directors` AND NOT (`the person is a shadow director, so that section 187(2) disapplies subsection (2)(a)`))
       OR `s 184 the notice in writing is in accordance with section 184` EQUALS JUST TRUE
       OR `s 185 the general notice is in accordance with section 185` EQUALS JUST TRUE
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE IF `s 184 the notice in writing is in accordance with section 184` EQUALS NOTHING OR `s 185 the general notice is in accordance with section 185` EQUALS NOTHING
         THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): whether the notice meets section 184 or section 185 is not known
         ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "The declaration must be made— (a) at a meeting of the directors, or (b) by notice in writing (see section 184), or (c) by general notice (see section 185)."

-- src:2420 | (3) If a declaration of interest under this section proves to be, or becomes, inaccurate or incomplete, a further declaration must be made.
@ref s 182(3) A further declaration (src:2420)
GIVEN `a declaration of interest under this section proves to be, or becomes, inaccurate or incomplete` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 182(3) a further declaration must be made` MEANS
    IF `a declaration of interest under this section proves to be, or becomes, inaccurate or incomplete`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "If a declaration of interest under this section proves to be, or becomes, inaccurate or incomplete, a further declaration must be made."

-- (4): "Any declaration required by this section must be made as soon as is reasonably practicable." No number of days: a
-- plain input. "Failure to comply with this requirement does not affect the underlying duty to make the declaration."
-- src:2421 | (4) Any declaration required by this section must be made as soon as is reasonably practicable.
@ref s 182(4) As soon as is reasonably practicable (src:2421)
GIVEN `the declaration was made as soon as was reasonably practicable` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 182(4) the declaration was made as soon as is reasonably practicable` MEANS
    IF `the declaration was made as soon as was reasonably practicable`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Any declaration required by this section must be made as soon as is reasonably practicable."

-- src:2422 | Failure to comply with this requirement does not affect the underlying duty to make the declaration.
@ref s 182(4) Failure does not affect the underlying duty (src:2422)
GIVEN `the director failed to comply with the requirement that the declaration be made as soon as is reasonably practicable` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 182(4) the failure affects the underlying duty to make the declaration` MEANS
    IF `the director failed to comply with the requirement that the declaration be made as soon as is reasonably practicable`
    THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Failure to comply with this requirement does not affect the underlying duty to make the declaration."
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the sentence speaks only of a failure to comply with the timing requirement

-- The director's compliance with s 182 as a whole: the declaration, in a way (2) allows and at the time (4) requires.
-- src:2413 | 182 Declaration of interest in existing transaction or arrangement
-- src:2414 | (1) Where a director of a company is in any way, directly or indirectly, interested in a transaction or arrangement that has been entered into by the company, he must declare the nature and extent of the interest to the other directors in accordance with this section.
-- src:2415 | This section does not apply if or to the extent that the interest has been declared under section 177 (duty to declare interest in proposed transaction or arrangement).
-- src:2416 | (2) The declaration must be made—
-- src:2417 | (a) at a meeting of the directors, or
-- src:2418 | (b) by notice in writing (see section 184), or
-- src:2419 | (c) by general notice (see section 185).
-- src:2421 | (4) Any declaration required by this section must be made as soon as is reasonably practicable.
@ref s 182(1), (2) and (4) The declaration made as the section requires (src:2413-2415 and src:2416-2419 and src:2421)
GIVEN `the answer under section 182(1)` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the director declared the nature and extent of the interest to the other directors` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the answer under section 182(2)` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the answer under section 182(4)` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 182 the director has complied with the requirements of section 182` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the answer under section 182(1)`
    WHEN JUST FALSE THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Any declaration required by this section"; no declaration is required
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): whether a declaration is required is not known
    WHEN JUST TRUE THEN
         IF NOT (`the director declared the nature and extent of the interest to the other directors`)
         THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "he must declare the nature and extent of the interest to the other directors in accordance with this section"
         ELSE IF `the answer under section 182(2)` EQUALS JUST FALSE OR `the answer under section 182(4)` EQUALS JUST FALSE
              THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "The declaration must be made"
              ELSE IF `the answer under section 182(2)` EQUALS JUST TRUE AND `the answer under section 182(4)` EQUALS JUST TRUE
                   THEN JUST TRUE
                   ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): whether the way or the time satisfies the section is not known

-- src:2413 | 182 Declaration of interest in existing transaction or arrangement
-- src:2414 | (1) Where a director of a company is in any way, directly or indirectly, interested in a transaction or arrangement that has been entered into by the company, he must declare the nature and extent of the interest to the other directors in accordance with this section.
-- src:2415 | This section does not apply if or to the extent that the interest has been declared under section 177 (duty to declare interest in proposed transaction or arrangement).
-- src:2421 | (4) Any declaration required by this section must be made as soon as is reasonably practicable.
@ref s 182(1) and (4) The director's duty to declare (regulative rule) (src:2413-2415 and src:2421)
`s 182 the director's duty to declare the interest to the other directors` MEANS
    PARTY Director
    MUST `Action of a party` OF Director, Director, "declare the nature and extent of the interest to the other directors as soon as is reasonably practicable"
    HENCE FULFILLED

-- ---- s 183: offence of failure to declare interest ---------------------------------------------------------------

-- src:2431 | 183 Offence of failure to declare interest
-- src:2432 | (1) A director who fails to comply with the requirements of section 182 (declaration of interest in existing transaction or arrangement) commits an offence.
@ref s 183(1) Offence of failure to declare interest (src:2431-2432)
GIVEN `the answer under section 182` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 183(1) the director commits an offence` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the answer under section 182`
    WHEN JUST FALSE THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN JUST TRUE THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "A director who fails to comply with the requirements of section 182 (declaration of interest in existing transaction or arrangement) commits an offence."
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): whether the director failed to comply with section 182 is not known

-- src:2433 | (2) A person guilty of an offence under this section is liable—
-- src:2434 | (a) on conviction on indictment, to a fine;
-- src:2435 | (b) on summary conviction, to a fine not exceeding the statutory maximum.
@ref s 183(2) Penalty for the offence (src:2433-2435)
GIVEN `how the person is convicted` IS A `Mode of conviction`
GIVETH A MAYBE Penalty
`s 183(2) the penalty for the offence` MEANS
    CONSIDER `how the person is convicted`
    WHEN `on conviction on indictment` THEN JUST (Penalty WITH
        `how convicted` IS `on conviction on indictment`
        `imprisonment not exceeding` IS NOTHING
        `fine not exceeding` IS JUST `a fine without a stated limit`
        `daily default fine for continued contravention` IS NOTHING
        `imprisonment and fine together` IS FALSE)
    WHEN `on summary conviction` THEN JUST (Penalty WITH
        `how convicted` IS `on summary conviction`
        `imprisonment not exceeding` IS NOTHING
        `fine not exceeding` IS JUST (`a fine not exceeding the statutory maximum` 1)
        `daily default fine for continued contravention` IS NOTHING
        `imprisonment and fine together` IS FALSE)
    OTHERWISE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the subsection states the penalty only on conviction on indictment and on summary conviction

-- ---- s 184: declaration made by notice in writing ----------------------------------------------------------------

-- src:2437 | (1) This section applies to a declaration of interest made by notice in writing.
@ref s 184(1) Declarations made by notice in writing (src:2437)
GIVEN `the declaration of interest is made by notice in writing` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 184(1) the section applies to the declaration` MEANS
    IF `the declaration of interest is made by notice in writing`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "This section applies to a declaration of interest made by notice in writing."

-- src:2438 | (2) The director must send the notice to the other directors.
@ref s 184(2) The director must send the notice to the other directors (src:2438)
GIVEN `the director sends the notice to the other directors` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 184(2) the director has sent the notice to the other directors` MEANS
    IF `the director sends the notice to the other directors`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "The director must send the notice to the other directors."

-- (3): "The notice may be sent in hard copy form or, if the recipient has agreed to receive it in electronic form, in an agreed
-- electronic form." The form is the core's `Form of document` (s 1168).
-- src:2439 | (3) The notice may be sent in hard copy form or, if the recipient has agreed to receive it in electronic form, in an agreed electronic form.
@ref s 184(3) The form of the notice (src:2439)
GIVEN form IS A `Form of document`
      `the recipient has agreed to receive it in electronic form` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the notice is in an agreed electronic form` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 184(3) the notice is sent in a form the subsection allows` MEANS
    CONSIDER form
    WHEN `hard copy form` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `electronic form` THEN IF `the recipient has agreed to receive it in electronic form` AND `the notice is in an agreed electronic form`
                                THEN JUST TRUE
                                ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "if the recipient has agreed to receive it in electronic form, in an agreed electronic form"

-- (4): "The notice may be sent (a) by hand or by post, or (b) if the recipient has agreed to receive it by electronic means, by
-- agreed electronic means."
DECLARE `s 184(4) means of sending the notice` IS ONE OF
    `s 184(4)(a) by hand`
    `s 184(4)(a) by post`
    `s 184(4)(b) by electronic means`
    `s 184(4) by another means`

-- src:2440 | (4) The notice may be sent—
-- src:2441 | (a) by hand or by post, or
-- src:2442 | (b) if the recipient has agreed to receive it by electronic means, by agreed electronic means.
@ref s 184(4) The means of sending the notice (src:2440-2442)
GIVEN means IS A `s 184(4) means of sending the notice`
      `the recipient has agreed to receive it by electronic means` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 184(4) the notice is sent by a means the subsection allows` MEANS
    CONSIDER means
    WHEN `s 184(4)(a) by hand` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `s 184(4)(a) by post` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `s 184(4)(b) by electronic means` THEN IF `the recipient has agreed to receive it by electronic means`
                                                  THEN JUST TRUE
                                                  ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "if the recipient has agreed to receive it by electronic means, by agreed electronic means"
    WHEN `s 184(4) by another means` THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (list not closed): "The notice may be sent"; the subsection permits and does not forbid another means

-- src:2443 | (5) Where a director declares an interest by notice in writing in accordance with this section—
-- src:2444 | (a) the making of the declaration is deemed to form part of the proceedings at the next meeting of the directors after the notice is given, and
@ref s 184(5)(a) The declaration is deemed part of the proceedings of the next meeting (src:2443-2444)
GIVEN `a director declares an interest by notice in writing in accordance with section 184` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 184(5)(a) the making of the declaration is deemed to form part of the proceedings at the next meeting of the directors after the notice is given` MEANS
    IF `a director declares an interest by notice in writing in accordance with section 184`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Where a director declares an interest by notice in writing in accordance with this section"

-- src:2443 | (5) Where a director declares an interest by notice in writing in accordance with this section—
-- src:2445 | (b) the provisions of section 248 (minutes of meetings of directors) apply as if the declaration had been made at that meeting.
@ref s 184(5)(b) Section 248 applies as if the declaration had been made at that meeting (src:2443 and src:2445)
GIVEN `a director declares an interest by notice in writing in accordance with section 184` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 184(5)(b) the provisions of section 248 apply as if the declaration had been made at that meeting` MEANS
    IF `a director declares an interest by notice in writing in accordance with section 184`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Where a director declares an interest by notice in writing in accordance with this section"

-- The notice in writing is "in accordance with section 184" when it is sent to the other directors (2), in a form (3) allows
-- and by a means (4) allows; the seam name is the one section 177(2) asks for.
-- src:2438 | (2) The director must send the notice to the other directors.
-- src:2439 | (3) The notice may be sent in hard copy form or, if the recipient has agreed to receive it in electronic form, in an agreed electronic form.
-- src:2440 | (4) The notice may be sent—
-- src:2441 | (a) by hand or by post, or
-- src:2442 | (b) if the recipient has agreed to receive it by electronic means, by agreed electronic means.
@ref s 184(2) to (4) A notice in writing in accordance with the section (src:2438-2442)
GIVEN `the answer under section 184(2)` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the answer under section 184(3)` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the answer under section 184(4)` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 184 the notice in writing is in accordance with section 184` MEANS
    IF `the answer under section 184(2)` EQUALS JUST FALSE OR `the answer under section 184(3)` EQUALS JUST FALSE OR `the answer under section 184(4)` EQUALS JUST FALSE
    THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "The director must send the notice to the other directors."
    ELSE IF `the answer under section 184(2)` EQUALS JUST TRUE AND `the answer under section 184(3)` EQUALS JUST TRUE AND `the answer under section 184(4)` EQUALS JUST TRUE
         THEN JUST TRUE
         ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (list not closed): the form or the means is one the subsection permits without saying it is the only one, or the facts are not known

-- ---- s 185: general notice treated as sufficient declaration -------------------------------------------------------

-- (2): general notice is notice given to the directors to the effect that the director (a) has an interest in a specified
-- body corporate or firm and is to be regarded as interested in any transaction or arrangement that may, after the date of
-- the notice, be made with it, or (b) is connected with a specified person (other than a body corporate or firm) and is to be
-- regarded as interested in any transaction or arrangement that may, after the date of the notice, be made with that person.
-- "connected with" is s 252 (coa5): a MAYBE BOOLEAN input.
-- src:2448 | (2) General notice is notice given to the directors of a company to the effect that the director—
-- src:2449 | (a) has an interest (as member, officer, employee or otherwise) in a specified body corporate or firm and is to be regarded as interested in any transaction or arrangement that may, after the date of the notice, be made with that body corporate or firm, or
-- src:2450 | (b) is connected with a specified person (other than a body corporate or firm) and is to be regarded as interested in any transaction or arrangement that may, after the date of the notice, be made with that person.
@ref s 185(2) General notice (src:2448-2450)
GIVEN `the notice is given to the directors to the effect that the director has an interest (as member, officer, employee or otherwise) in a specified body corporate or firm and is to be regarded as interested in any transaction or arrangement that may, after the date of the notice, be made with that body corporate or firm` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the notice is given to the directors to the effect that the director is connected with a specified person (other than a body corporate or firm) and is to be regarded as interested in any transaction or arrangement that may, after the date of the notice, be made with that person` IS A BOOLEAN
      `s 252 the specified person is connected with the director` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 185(2) the notice is general notice` MEANS
    IF `the notice is given to the directors to the effect that the director has an interest (as member, officer, employee or otherwise) in a specified body corporate or firm and is to be regarded as interested in any transaction or arrangement that may, after the date of the notice, be made with that body corporate or firm`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE IF `the notice is given to the directors to the effect that the director is connected with a specified person (other than a body corporate or firm) and is to be regarded as interested in any transaction or arrangement that may, after the date of the notice, be made with that person`
         THEN CONSIDER `s 252 the specified person is connected with the director`
              WHEN JUST TRUE THEN JUST TRUE
              WHEN JUST FALSE THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "(b) is connected with a specified person (other than a body corporate or firm)"
              WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): whether the person is connected with the director is s 252 (coa5)
         ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "General notice is notice given to the directors of a company to the effect that the director"

-- src:2451 | (3) The notice must state the nature and extent of the director's interest in the body corporate or firm or, as the case may be, the nature of his connection with the person.
@ref s 185(3) What the notice must state (src:2451)
GIVEN `the notice states the nature and extent of the director's interest in the body corporate or firm or, as the case may be, the nature of his connection with the person` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 185(3) the notice states what the subsection requires` MEANS
    IF `the notice states the nature and extent of the director's interest in the body corporate or firm or, as the case may be, the nature of his connection with the person`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "The notice must state the nature and extent of the director's interest in the body corporate or firm or, as the case may be, the nature of his connection with the person."

-- (4): "General notice is not effective unless (a) it is given at a meeting of the directors, or (b) the director takes reasonable
-- steps to secure that it is brought up and read at the next meeting of the directors after it is given." The function says
-- whether the subsection makes the notice ineffective (JUST TRUE = it does not yet satisfy (a) or (b)). Section 187(3) takes the
-- shadow director's general notice out of subsection (4).
-- src:2452 | (4) General notice is not effective unless—
-- src:2453 | (a) it is given at a meeting of the directors, or
-- src:2454 | (b) the director takes reasonable steps to secure that it is brought up and read at the next meeting of the directors after it is given.
@ref s 185(4) General notice is not effective unless (src:2452-2454)
GIVEN `the general notice is given at a meeting of the directors` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the director takes reasonable steps to secure that it is brought up and read at the next meeting of the directors after it is given` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is a shadow director, so that section 187(3) disapplies subsection (4)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 185(4) section 185(4) makes the general notice ineffective` MEANS
